# SQLite: what the adaptation cost beside the allocator, for I1.
# One line per file: <path>  <bucket>  <why>. Buckets: allocator, compat, glue, test.
#
# The allocator itself is sublet/sublet-3530300.patch, counted by port-effort.py against
# its own .classes file and not recounted here. That patch covers BOTH of SQLite's
# allocators, lookaside and memsys5, and I1 says not to split it without a validated
# classification, so this ledger does not split it either.
#
# READ THE TEST BUCKET CAREFULLY. It is nine thousand lines, and 7 306 of them are
# sqlite_capstone_domain.c, which accumulated a probe per compiler and RTL question over the whole
# bring-up. That is the history of getting SQLite onto this hardware, not the cost of adapting its
# allocator. The buckets exist so the two cannot be read as one number.

adapted/capstone_sqlite_libc.c                 compat   the libc SQLite calls and a domain has none of
adapted/capstone_sqlite_libc.h                 compat   the libc SQLite calls and a domain has none of
adapted/capstone_sqlite_os.c                   compat   the VFS SQLITE_OS_OTHER leaves to the port
adapted/capstone_sqlite_stdio.c                compat   the formatting SQLite calls and a domain has none of
adapted/capstone_sqlite_stdio.h                compat   the formatting SQLite calls and a domain has none of
adapted/stubinc/assert.h                       compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/ctype.h                        compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/math.h                         compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/stdio.h                        compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/stdlib.h                       compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/string.h                       compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/sys/types.h                    compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/time.h                         compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
adapted/stubinc/unistd.h                       compat   a header the freestanding build needs to exist and not to do anything
capstone_floatdidf_noglobals.c                 compat   one libgcc routine rewritten without globals, which gp-captable forbids
probes/local-cap-aggregate.c                   test     one probe each for a compiler or RTL question
probes/nested-cap-global.c                     test     one probe each for a compiler or RTL question
probes/runtime-bytecopy-capability.c           test     one probe each for a compiler or RTL question
revoke_on_free_alloc.h                         glue     the revoke-on-free arm the reuse experiment compares against
revoke_on_free_hier_alloc.h                    glue     the revoke-on-free arm the reuse experiment compares against
slt/slt_md5.h                                  test     the sqllogictest runner, upstream's own correctness suite
slt/slt_native.c                               test     the sqllogictest runner, upstream's own correctness suite
slt/slt_runner.h                               test     the sqllogictest runner, upstream's own correctness suite
speedtest1_baseline.c                          test     SQLite's own benchmark, the workload both arms run
speedtest1_domain.c                            test     SQLite's own benchmark, the workload both arms run
speedtest1_measure.c                           test     SQLite's own benchmark, the workload both arms run
sqlite_boundary_cost_domain.c                  test     the boundary-cost probe
sqlite_capstone_domain.c                       test     the domain the reuse experiment runs in
sqlite_host.c                                  test     the guest that creates the domain
sqlite_host_row3.c                             test     the guest that creates the domain
sqlite_host_row3_b2.c                          test     the guest that creates the domain
sqlite_hostcall.h                              glue     what the guest and the domain agree to call each other
sqlite_row11_domain.c                          test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row14_domain.c                          test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row2_domain.c                           test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row3_b2_domain.c                        test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row3_domain.c                           test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row5_domain.c                           test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row7_domain.c                           test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_row9_domain.c                           test     one image per row of the experiment matrix
sqlite_silicon_amalgam.c                       glue     the amalgamation the silicon build links, one translation unit

sublet/sublet-3530300.patch               allocator  the classified patch, counted by port-effort.py, and it covers BOTH allocators
